Most of the postings I've been seeing lately are from the NetHackGods,
who are pleased with NH3 because it finally puts something of a challenge
back into the game for them.  Even still, some of them appear to be
getting their first wins within a few weeks of getting the code.

For new players and inexperienced players, however, the game is nigh
unbeatable.  Monsters are tougher, hit harder, and don't leave edible
corpses very often.  New features (like not being able to #sacrifice
except at altars) make some of the old tricks harder to put into 
practice.  Players who were used to striding confidently through the
Dungeon are now lucky to make it down to Dlevel 3 without starving or
being killed by one hit from a monster they used to feel only moderately
nervous about.  For these players, the game is not fun, or even a challenge,
only frustrating.

Now, many experienced players will doubtless reply, "You just have to learn
the tricks and play intelligently.  You'll get it sooner or later."  Fine--
but in the meantime, players who have just discovered the game in its third
incarnation will turn away in disgust and frustration without ever going
through this learning process.  The same is true of many intermediate players,
like myself, who know many of the tricks but have never gotten past Dlevel 10
on NH2.3, and don't play with the goal of winning.

If this process of upgrading the difficulty of the game to make it challenging
for the expert players continues, I see the risk of making it impossible to
enter from the ground level.  This hazard is increased by the fact that many
sites routinely delete the old versions of games like NetHack, so that only  
the most recent (and advanced/difficult) version is available.

It may be that players who can win NetHack on a regular basis should take
this as a sign of accomplishment and outgrowing of the game, and should
move on to more difficult ones rather than pushing up the level of experience
required to enter the game.  Also, remember that some players don't play for
the Amulet, but simply see what fortune will give them.


